  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The correct statements from the following are:</p><p>A. The strength of anionic ligands can be explained by crystal field theory.</p><p>B. Valence bond theory does not give a quantitative interpretation of kinetic stability of coordination compounds.</p><p>C. The hybridization involved in formation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi>Ni</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CN</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>]</mo><msup><mo> </mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>–</mo></mrow></msup></math> complex is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>dsp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p><p>D. The number of possible isomer(s) of cis-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>PtCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo> </mo><mo>(</mo><mi>en</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>]</mo><msup><mo> </mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> is one</p><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "0QK0i",
      "text": "A, D only",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gGlWC",
